{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in last night with vomiting and abdominal pain during your tube feed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started around 10:30 PM. I was on my usual feed, but suddenly got sharp pain and started vomiting. It felt just like my last flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. No fever, chills, or blood in the vomit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. My J-tube is clear, and I’ve had bowel movements. It’s just the pain and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring. Your exam shows mild tenderness but no signs of blockage. We checked labs—your bicarbonate is a bit low at 19, and lactate is slightly elevated at 2.3, which suggests mild dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I’ve been having these flares more often lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not dangerous right now. The dehydration is mild. We’re giving you IV fluids and medications to calm your stomach—Zofran, Reglan, Ativan, and a little morphine for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s the same combo that helped before. I hope it works again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-04-20 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it usually does. We’ll keep your tube feeds off for now and restart slowly once you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-04-20 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling now? Any nausea or pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-04-20 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little tired, but the pain is much better. I haven’t vomited since last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-04-20 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your repeat vitals are stable—BP 112/73, pulse 81. We’ll start clear liquids by mouth and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-04-20 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-04-20 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to make sure you can keep fluids down and tolerate your tube feeds again. This usually takes a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well with clear liquids. We’re going to restart your J-tube feeds at a low rate—68 mL/hr—for the night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought we slowed it to 90 before. Is 68 safer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we lowered it from 90 to see if that reduced flares. But this episode happened even at 68, so we’re not sure the rate is the only factor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing them then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your gastroparesis is idiopathic—no clear cause. No diabetes, no nerve damage, no cancer. The gastric emptying scan showed 48% retention at 4 hours, which confirms delayed emptying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And there’s nothing else they can do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "At this point, the focus is on managing symptoms. You’re followed by Dr. Patel at the GI clinic—they’ve said no further interventions are likely to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wish it didn’t keep happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-04-20 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll keep using the same meds that work—ondansetron, Tigan, lorazepam as needed. And stay hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-04-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You made it through the night without vomiting. Your labs this morning look better—bicarbonate still 19, but kidney function is normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-04-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-04-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. First, we’ll increase your tube feeds back to your regular rate and watch you for a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-04-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds? I take levothyroxine at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-04-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve been giving it every night. Your thyroid levels are stable, so no changes needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-04-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re going to do a formal enteral feeding infusion at 90 mL/hr now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-04-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try. No nausea so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-04-21 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you tolerated the full feed without issues. We’re on track for discharge tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-04-21 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been so anxious about these flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-04-21 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. Your anxiety and depression are being managed with citalopram and lorazepam as needed. Keep using them as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-04-21 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I have my appointment with Dr. Patel in two weeks?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-04-21 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. They’ll monitor your gastroparesis long-term. No changes to your other meds—vitamin D, omeprazole, all stay the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Final check—you’re still feeling well, no pain or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel much better. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your discharge labs are stable. We’ll send you home with instructions to continue your meds and follow up with Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use your PRN meds—ondansetron, Tigan, lorazepam. If it doesn’t settle within a few hours, call your doctor or come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-04-22 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get the discharge papers ready. You should be out by 10 AM."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-04-20 07:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-04-22 10:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of idiopathic gastroparesis and J-tube placement was admitted for a flare characterized by sudden abdominal pain and vomiting during a tube feed. She had no signs of infection, obstruction, or metabolic instability. Treatment included IV fluids, antiemetics (ondansetron, prochlorperazine), Ativan, and morphine, with gradual reintroduction of tube feeds. She tolerated full feeds at 90 mL/hr and remained symptom-free, leading to discharge home after two days. Her hypothyroidism was stable on levothyroxine, and all other chronic conditions were managed without change. Follow-up was arranged with her gastroenterologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Unspecified vitamin D deficiency",
      "Attention to other artificial opening of digestive tract",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Irritable bowel syndrome",
      "Osteoporosis, unspecified",
      "Intestinal disaccharidase deficiencies and disaccharide malabsorption"
    ]
  }
}
